["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"aep","stream_identity":"01a0cae6-7e88-710c-8913-d70d29cb7b4c","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"aep.entity","fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"MIG871268dedac3afe3a6efca5ae259750d68c8daed59650bae0d7ebadf38eb3848","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/postgres-advisory-lock-runtime-pin","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":7,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"## Context\n\nA live central-service run found that Entity Runtime 0.17.1 injected a NUL into every absent-identity advisory lock. After that correction, the first live EP indexed lookup exposed a second provider binding defect. ER 0.17.3 corrects both boundaries, but EP's released fresh-session backend continues to compile against the faulty generation until EP republishes its coordinated pin.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nEvery EP Entity Runtime dependency resolves to 0.17.3, the fresh PostgreSQL command-session conformance test passes against a live server, and a patch release makes that dependency generation consumable by aep-service.\n\n## Implementation\n\nThe workspace now resolves every Entity Runtime dependency from tag 0.17.3. EP's fresh PostgreSQL command session therefore uses valid pairwise advisory-lock hashing and text-to-JSONB containment binding without changing EP's semantic or wire contracts.\n","relations":[{"serves":"vision:O2"}],"status":"implemented","summary":"Publish the fresh command session against Entity Runtime's corrected text lock key.","title":"Adopt valid PostgreSQL advisory locks"},"lifecycle_state":"implemented"}},"id":"MIG871268dedac3afe3a6efca5ae259750d68c8daed59650bae0d7ebadf38eb3848","lifecycle_state":"recorded","revision":7,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["aep.entity","MIG871268dedac3afe3a6efca5ae259750d68c8daed59650bae0d7ebadf38eb3848